id: bag-of-senzu-beans
name: Bag of Senzu Beans
kind: gear
# A Special Basic Item: "cannot be obtained by Crafting and can only be gained from your ARC".
# No Craft DC, since nothing makes it.
special: true
# "Bags of Senzu Beans come in various sizes" - asked when it is given, and rolled.
sizes: Small=1d4, Standard=1d6, Large=1d10, Extra Large=2d6
chargesLabel: Senzu Beans
# "You can spend 1 Action to consume a Senzu Bean or feed it to an adjacent, Defeated
# Character."
placeCost: 1
feedsDefeated: true
# "Consuming a Senzu Bean removes all Combat Conditions (except Pinned or Suffocating) and you
# fully regain your Life and Ki Points, up to their maximum."
restoresFully: true
restoreKeeps: pinned, suffocating
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Bean for an Action, eaten or fed to a Defeated friend beside you: every Combat Condition
  but Pinned and Suffocating gone, and Life and Ki full.
text: >
  Bag of Senzu Beans: A bag containing the miraculous Senzu Beans.
  –Effects: You can spend 1 Action to consume a Senzu Bean or feed it to an adjacent, Defeated
  Character. Consuming a Senzu Bean removes all Combat Conditions (except Pinned or
  Suffocating) and you fully regain your Life and Ki Points, up to their maximum.

  Bags of Senzu Beans come in various sizes:

  * Small. Roll a 1d4, that’s how many Senzu Beans are in the bag.
  * Standard. Roll a 1d6, that’s how many Senzu Beans are in the bag.
  * Large. Roll a solid 1d10, that’s how many Senzu Beans are in the bag.
  * Extra Large. Roll a 2d6, that’s how many Senzu Beans are in the bag.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Given: the size is asked and its Beans rolled - the count shown on the row and editable on
# the Item.
#
# Eat: 1 Action and 1 Bean. Every Combat Condition comes off but Pinned and Suffocating - the
# marks this system keeps under the same folder are not Combat Conditions, and stay - and
# Life and Ki are set to their maximum.
#
# Feed: the same, for the one character targeted, who has to be Defeated and adjacent -
# measured on the map, and not enforced where nothing can be measured. Full Life is what
# stands a Defeated character back up: Defeated is having no Life left.
#
# An empty bag stays on the character, for the player to take off or the ARC to refill.
